   {
    "attributes": [
     {
      "_key": "5r5sFjSBWMIetVQk4N5EFc",
      "name": "Why I'm standing",
      "value": "I'm running for election in 2026 because at 30 years old I was made redundant and could not find a job, and so many people in NZ are in the same boat. I'm a student, the cost of living is high, things are tough and New Zealanders deserve better. Our economy has relied on unfairly taxing working people for far too long, it's time for tax equity and a government that works for us."
     },
     {
      "_key": "5r5sFjSBWMIetVQk4N5EKq",
      "name": "About me",
      "value": "I would make a good elected representative for ilam because I'm a regular working kiwi who understands the struggle because I am living the struggle. I grew up in Redwood, went to Burnside High School and know the Ilam area very well. There's lots of families and students that are doing all they can to make ends meet and are still struggling. I will advocate for you because I am you."
     },
     {
      "_key": "5r5sFjSBWMIetVQk4N5EQ4",
      "name": "Priority 1",
      "value": "Tax reform - shifting the tax burden off work and onto wealth, delivering tax relief to workers"
     },
     {
      "_key": "5r5sFjSBWMIetVQk4N5EVI",
      "name": "Priority 2",
      "value": "Full Employment - Roll out our policy for a genuine reduction in unemployment nationwide."
     },
     {
      "_key": "5r5sFjSBWMIetVQk4N5EaW",
      "name": "Priority 3",
      "value": "Integrated Infrastructure & Transport Plan - introduce KiwiWorks to build our needed infrastructure"
     }
    ],
